{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"The AWS review-bot holds a persistent tickets clone that a redeploy does not refresh, and it writes on every Gerrit vote. Make the clone self-converge after the epoch guard has landed, and fix the deploy path so later ensure-script changes reach the box automatically. Session log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** contains the measured facts.\n\n## Why\n\nThe clone lives on the EBS-backed external volume declared in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`. The generated entrypoint in `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:127-149` clones only when `${REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_DIR}/.git` is absent, so a normal redeploy preserves any divergent history. The entrypoint invokes `reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` outside the PAT block, so convergence must still run when `REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_PAT` is unset.\n\n`infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh:50-69` currently configures the repo-local identity and runs the ensure registry, but does not fetch, classify ancestry, or reset a divergent persistent clone. The bot uses `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`; its artifact writer runs after the Gerrit vote and catches store errors inside `src/rebar/review_bot/artifact_emit.py:56-166`, while the call site is `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:719`. Convergence failure must remain best-effort and must never undo or wedge an already-cast vote.\n\n## Deployment bootstrap\n\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:90` omits `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` from `BOT_PATHS`. The deploy decision at `:276` and rsync at `:334` therefore cannot deliver a first commit that changes only these scripts. This ticket depends on A6-0a and lands **after A6-0a**, as its own independently reviewable Gerrit change.\n\nAfter this scripts-only change merges, perform the documented one-time hand-deploy from `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md`: update `/var/lib/rebar/mirror`, install the merged `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` into `/opt/rebar` while preserving owner `502:502`, and start `rebar-autodeploy.service`. The newly installed `BOT_PATHS` then detects the ensure-script change and performs the normal rsync/build/health workflow. Future ensure-script changes self-deploy without another bootstrap.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. In `reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh`, fetch `origin/tickets` and classify the persistent clone:\n   - equal or local strictly ahead: keep the local tip;\n   - local behind: fast-forward/reset to `origin/tickets`;\n   - histories diverged: reset hard to `origin/tickets`.\n   The reset is permitted only for this dedicated review-bot clone, whose writes use synchronous `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`; log the old and new tips for the operator receipt.\n2. Add `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` to `autodeploy.sh` `BOT_PATHS`.\n3. Preserve execution outside the PAT block and preserve best-effort vote safety.\n4. Hand-bootstrap the first deployment after merge, then record the deployed main SHA or image digest, the successful autodeploy/health receipt, a deployed-runtime epoch-mismatch refusal probe, and the persistent-clone convergence result.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Given real temporary clones with divergent local and `origin/tickets` histories, the ensure script resets the dedicated review-bot clone to `origin/tickets`, leaves no local-only commit, and logs both tips. Tier: shell integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Given an equal, merely-behind, or strictly-ahead clone, equal/ahead tips are preserved and a behind clone converges to `origin/tickets`; no case leaves merge or stash state. Tier: shell integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] With `REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_PAT` unset, the ensure/convergence invocation remains outside the PAT block and executes against an existing clone. Tier: shell integration through the generated entrypoint.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` appears in `autodeploy.sh` `BOT_PATHS`, and a path-classifier test proves a change to that script selects the review-bot deploy branch.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An injected rebar store write failure after `post_vote` still leaves the Gerrit vote recorded and returns through the existing best-effort artifact path. Tier: unit at the artifact/caller boundary.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The merged A6-0b SHA or image digest, one-time hand-bootstrap command exits, successful autodeploy/health receipt, deployed-runtime epoch-mismatch refusal output, and persistent-clone convergence old/new tips are recorded on this ticket before closure.\n\n## Files\n\n`infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh`, `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`, `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot` tests only if required for generated-entrypoint coverage, and focused tests.\n\nScope: S. Depends on A6-0a; lands after A6-0a as its own change."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785816647748240001,"uuid":"97d818e4-33e0-4307-a67f-f1eeb544a34e"}